python-mcp (1:2.0.0~b2-1~vitex1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update to upstream v2.0.0b2 (v2.0 line), overriding the 1:1.27.1-1
    revert below: development of the v2 line resumed and has since
    reached rc1 upstream (2.0.0b2 is what fastmcp 4.0.0a2's own
    fastmcp-slim package hard-pins as its exact mcp requirement).
    Keep epoch 1: so this still supersedes 1:1.27.1 by version
    comparison; add a ~vitex1 local suffix as this is a local,
    non-archive build for the mcprack fastmcp 4.0.0a2 migration.
  * debian/control: replace python3-httpx/python3-httpx-sse with
    python3-httpx2 (upstream moved to httpx2 in this release, see
    upstream commit "Replace httpx and httpx-sse with httpx2" #2972);
    add python3-mcp-types (= 2.0.0~b2) and
    python3-opentelemetry-api (>= 1.28.0), both new dependencies in
    this release; bump python3-anyio to >= 4.9, python3-pydantic to
    >= 2.12.0, python3-sse-starlette to >= 3.0.0,
    python3-typing-extensions to >= 4.13.0 to match.
  * pyproject.toml: statically resolve the upstream dynamic version
    and dynamic (metadata-hook-templated) dependencies list, since the
    uv-dynamic-versioning hatchling metadata hook plugin isn't
    packaged for Debian; mirrors debian/rules' existing
    override_dh_auto_configure approach for the plain dynamic-version
    case, extended here to also cover dynamic dependencies.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:45:00 +0200

